<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Calculate Data_Size depending on Port_Process_Data_Size input by the user]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQ(Port_Process_Data_Size,0) MOVE(1,Data_Size) ,EQ(Port_Process_Data_Size,1) MOVE(2,Data_Size) ,EQ(Port_Process_Data_Size,2) MOVE(4,Data_Size) ,EQ(Port_Process_Data_Size,3) MOVE(8,Data_Size) ,EQ(Port_Process_Data_Size,4) MOVE(16,Data_Size) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the user input Port_Number <= to the maximum number of ports on the IO-Link master (4 or 8) and the Port_Number != to 0 then 
calculate the Process_Offset  (if process input data is produced by the IO-Link Device) and/or calculate the Process_Value_Offset (if process output data is consumed by the IO-Link Device). 
Parallel to the Calculation of the Process_Offset and/or Process_Value_Offset calculate the value of the StatusFlgs_Offset
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LE(Port_Number,8)GT(Port_Number,0)SUB(Port_Number,1,RealPort_Num)[MUL(Data_Size,RealPort_Num,Offset_Address) ADD(Offset_Address,95,Process_Offset) ,MUL(9,RealPort_Num,Offset_StatusFlgs) ADD(Offset_StatusFlgs,23,StatusFlgs_Offset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Sets states of IOL_Mode, Device_Not_Connected, Invalid_Data, Wrong_VID_DID and Diagnostic Available and set the values for the Vendor ID and Device ID from the Controller input tags of the user input Port_Number
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PLC_Input[StatusFlgs_Offset].0) OTE(IOL_Mode) ,XIC(PLC_Input[StatusFlgs_Offset].1) OTE(Device_Not_Connected) ,XIC(PLC_Input[StatusFlgs_Offset].2) OTE(Invalid_Data) ,XIC(PLC_Input[StatusFlgs_Offset].3) OTE(Wrong_VID_DID) ,XIC(PLC_Input[StatusFlgs_Offset].7) OTE(Diagnostic_Avail) ,MOVE(PLC_Input[StatusFlgs_Offset+1],Vendor_ID) ,COP(PLC_Input[StatusFlgs_Offset+2],Device_ID,1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Set the State of AOI_Setting_Error by verifying the user input setting of Port_Number and Port_Process_Data_Size is within range of the IO-Link Master. GRT instruction for Port_Number compares to value=8 for 8 port masters and =4 for 4 port masters]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LE(Port_Number,0) ,GT(Port_Number,8) ,LT(Port_Process_Data_Size,0) ,GT(Port_Process_Data_Size,4) ]OTE(AOI_Settings_Error);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Logic for the IO-Link device’s producing and/or consuming process data. Device Status Information is not included]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOVE(PLC_Input[Process_Offset],Intensity) ,XIC(PLC_Input[Process_Offset+1].0) OTE(SSC1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Device Status byte is converted to binary outputs]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[BTD(PLC_Input[Process_Offset+1],4,Device_Status,0,4)[EQ(Device_Status,0) OTE(Device_OK) ,EQ(Device_Status,1) OTE(Maintenance_required) ,EQ(Device_Status,2) OTE(Out_Of_Specification) ,EQ(Device_Status,3) OTE(Functional_check) ,EQ(Device_Status,4) OTE(Failure) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Name="ProgramAlarmHandler" Class="Standard" Revision="3.0" Vendor="Steven Douglas Corp." ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2017-08-23T18:02:02.410Z" CreatedBy="STEVENDOUGLAS\dshaner" EditedDate="2022-07-08T15:33:47.239Z" EditedBy="STEVENDOUGLAS\wehamby"
 SoftwareRevision="v34.00">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Creates a shared Alarm History array and a shared Active Alarms array.]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[v3.0 : 2022-06-16 D.E.S. Added Alarm Group to the AlarmData UDT.]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[This AOI works in conjuction with the Alarms Porgram.

ControllerProgramIDTag needs to be the exact same tag for all instances of this AOI in your project.This AOI then uses that tag to uniquely identify each instance of the AOI in your project.

LocalAlarmsArrayTag is where you define each alarm for this AOI. Type in your Message and set the Severity when you create a new alarm. Severity is used on the HMI for coloring - found in the Alarm Display AOG background object's animation.

Use output coils or latches on the Active bit to trigger the alarm.

If you set DoNotSaveToHistory it will prevent the alarm from being put in the Alarm History array.

HMIActiveArrayTag and HMIHistoryArrayTag are arrays of the AlarmData UDT. They are shared by all instances of this AOI.

Alarm History is updated when an alarm becomes inactive so the Duration can be saved.

Changelog:
v3.0 : 2022-06-16 D.E.S. Added Alarm Group to the AlarmData UDT.
v2.3a: 2022-06-16 D.E.S. For Beckett. Severity MOD 200 because of different zones
v2.3 : 2022-06-14 D.E.S. Sort displayed alarm list by severity
v2.2 : 2022-01-03 D.E.S. Don't add alarm to active array if full.
v2.1 : 2021-05-11 D.E.S. Use UTC for date.
v2.0 : 2019-12-12 D.E.S. variable array lengths!
v1.2 : 2018-06-03 W.E.H. Changed NoFault to Faulted
v1.1 : 2017-09-12 W.E.H.
v1.0 : 2017-08-24 D.E.S.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
