<Routine Name="Outputs" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[NOTES: 
The EstopGuardOK bits are used to turn on the outputs or enable devices. The SafeOK bits should be used in the logic that controls the outputs/devices. There is a purposeful delay from when the outputs are turned on to when the logic can proceed to start controlling the outputs/devices. this delay allows the device hardware to power up or get ready to receive commands from the ladder logic.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(EStopOK)XIC(AllGuardDoorsClosed)OTE(AirDumpValveEnergize);]]>
